The DLLs in numj/native/windows-x86_64/ were compiled from native/*.f90 of https://github.com/hareramray/numj with
GCC/gfortran 16.2.0 (WinLibs MinGW-w64 UCRT r2) and statically linked with the GCC runtime libraries (libgfortran,
libgomp, libgcc, and libquadmath where libgfortran uses it). Those libraries are licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 with the
GCC Runtime Library Exception, version 3.1, which permits distributing code linked with them under licence terms of
your choice: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gcc-exception-3.1.html
The DLLs also link dynamically against the Windows Universal C Runtime (UCRT), which is part of Windows.

  x86-64-v3/numj.dll   -O3 -march=x86-64-v3 -ffp-contract=off  (AVX2/FMA CPUs; Haswell 2013 / Excavator 2015 or newer)
  baseline/numj.dll    -O3 -march=x86-64    -ffp-contract=off  (any x86-64 CPU)
Both give bitwise-identical results. numj chooses one at load time (override: -Dnumj.cpu=baseline).
